									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/heroman3003" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7041432); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7041432&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606030425" alt="Heroman3003" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7041432)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/heroman3003" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7041432); return false;" >Heroman3003</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606029788 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Nov 2020 07:23</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13870498/alternative-classification-system-seeking-greenlight">Alternative Classification System (Seeking Greenlight)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825243">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article (potentially -J if idea is decided to be too silly/meta by reviewers)</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Comedy</p>
<strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A connection on the internal Foundation database with unknown source that leads to a database of documented SCP Objects that is mostly identical to foundation's own, with key difference being that classification system used for SCP types is different. Connection severs itself and immedeately reinstates every 24 hours, connecting to a different alternative database. In addition to that, any attempt at documenting the SCP itself results in it changing its own classification to match whatever system is used in current connection.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The connection is direct and two-way, but read-only veiw into a tiny glimpse of life of Foundation in alternate reality. Due to nature of the SCP all realities remain the same in terms of amount of knowledge on SCPs themselves and state of foundation, with extremely rare exceptions. However, differences in things unrelated to SCPs themselves are fairly common, if hard to find due to nature of the materials being accessed. In addition, all the access restrictions are still perfectly functional, so researcher in charge of the SCP cannot access any particularly classified one without direct permission. Through continuous observation, Foundation also finds very minor ways to enchance its performance, though again, in fields unrelated to the handling or finding SCPs themselves.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Primarily, the article would be a list of various alternative systems of classification recorded, ranging from reasonable to completely absurd to downright esoteric. Regular notes about differences that aren't the system itself would also allow it to not be excessively repetitive.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<strong>Additional Notes:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The focus will mostly be lighthearted moreso than comedic, if it is approved as regular article. Main inspiration for the article has been growth of use of esoteric SCP Classes in recent articles, and its meant to be a light little meta reference to that, while still being reasonable as a standalone thing.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

