					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3460794); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3460794&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606030425" alt="Kothardarastrix" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3460794)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3460794); return false;" >Kothardarastrix</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606029473 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Nov 2020 07:17</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-88827/foundation-universe">SCP Universe / Foundation Universe</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13870480/i-love-the-lolfoundation">I LOVE the lolfoundation</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825239">
									

<p>Well, everyone doesn't &quot;have a problem&quot; with it, they just don't like when it intrudes on works intended to be serious. lolfoundation has its own separate canon so all the wacky shenanigans can take place over there without intruding on the supreme horror of the 3000-contest entries or what have you. Articles written to create more of a serious tone are completely ruined by things like demotion to D-class and wacky addenda, which break most people's suspension of belief because an organization like the Foundation wouldn't really be so careless. In general, I think most of the website's users come here for horror, which doesn't mesh great with wacky shenanigans. Like I said, though, there's a whole separate canon for lolfoundation. There aren't a whole lot of comparable shenanigans going on in most mainlist articles, but a few gems like <a href="/scp-4444">SCP-4444</a> and <a href="/scp-5004">SCP-5004</a> do still feature the senior staff being funny. Also, the Resurrection canon also has some elements of lolfoundation in it - Duke 'til Dawn and Incident 239-B really happened in Resurrection, and comparable things (within reason) can still happen to an extent.</p>
<p>tl;dr funny Foundation is still a thing, it's just separated out from regular Foundation more than it used to be.</p>

