														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825214">
									

<p>Hey there Cesss, I'll be critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am not a particularly experienced nor official reviewer (like the others here), so take what I say with a grain of salt. With that being said, let's begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Elevator Pitch</span></p>
<p>I'm going to be honest, I don't really like this idea. All it is is a random gas station that, for some reason, has mirrors that cause your reflection to take control of you and then kill you. Why? Are the reflections like some kind of demon or something? This just seems like a less interesting/creative version of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-919">SCP-919</a>, which presents a moral/ethical dilemma over whether the reflections are animate or not, rather than a reflection that just kills you.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Central Narrative</span></p>
<p>This narrative is&#8230; adequate, but I still don't like the concept behind it. It just isn't interesting enough for me to have a random gas station mirror with murderous, possessive reflections. There is also a logistical problem behind your narrative: how did the Foundation find this footage? Unless there was a camera on the Researcher's body (extremely unlikely), there is no way they could have information this detailed on the Researcher's death.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Hook/Attention Grabber</span></p>
<p>So the gas station moves and people start swapping consciousnesses their own reflections. That's it. The swapping part could be interesting if explored more, but the gas station (and the fact that it moves) seems&#8230; disjointed. Why are the reflections part of a gas station? Why does the gas station move?</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>At the moment, your idea would likely be downvoted by members of this Site (myself included) if it became an article, mostly due to a lack of substance. This lack of substance takes the form of:<br />
- A boring/uncreative anomaly<br />
- Little story<br />
- The slightly disjointed/random nature of the separate parts of the anomaly<br />
- The fact it is a 'thing that kills you' SCP (a common trope on this Site, whereby the anomaly is simply something that kills you without much backstory or substance)<br />
Simply put, this idea isn't <em>interesting</em> enough. All it is a killer reflection in a random, moving gas station. Now, if this were reflections trying to take over their 'real' counterparts (i.e switch bodies with them) and having identity crises, I'd be interested. Hearing the tale of a scientist who lost their body and gained it back after hunting their eisoptrophobic (afraid of mirrors) reflection and cornering them in a room with a mirror (idk, that's just a story I came up with. You can use it, if you want) is interesting to me. As it stands, this is just effectively an anomalous murderer. The end.</p>
<p>I'd recommend two things:<br />
1. Check out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for some great ideation/narrative creation advice!<br />
2. Contact reviewers from the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get some experienced alternative opinions!</p>
<p>And finally, to sum up your idea in one sentence<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-313605-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-313605-1')">1</a></sup>:<br />
Moving gas station has mirrors which cause your reflection to possess you and make you kill yourself.</p>
<p>Just some things for you to <em>reflect</em> on.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Anyway, that's about it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and hopefully this helps!
